# eSMART credentials -- normally written AUTOMATICALLY during setup:
#   * the web page  http://127.0.0.1:8090/pair  (double-click "Start eSMART"), or
#   * the terminal:  python3 esmart.py pair
# You only edit this file by hand for manual / advanced setups.
# SECRET: copy this to .esmart.env and never commit that file (it is
# git-ignored and written mode 600).
#
# The pairing code is NOT stored here and is NOT the password. It is shown once
# on the tablet, valid for about a minute, and only used to make the central
# accept this account. Both values below are generated locally and this client
# creates the account itself with XMPP in-band registration, exactly like the
# iOS app does:
#   ESMART_JID      "i-<13 random chars>-<111..999>@myesmart.net"
#   ESMART_PASSWORD 15 random chars
ESMART_JID=i-exampleexample-123@myesmart.net
ESMART_PASSWORD=replacewithrand0m
ESMART_XMPP_HOST=xmpp.myesmart.net
ESMART_XMPP_PORT=5222
# The central joins us as <its MAC>@myesmart.net and that MAC is the house MUC
# room, written here automatically after pairing. ESMART_ROOM overrides it.
# ESMART_ROOM=00-00-87-01-03-01-58
